You are implementing the Dynamic Layers System redesign for this SuperCollider project.

## Your Task
Implement the approved dynamic layer-per-VST-group architecture, replacing the hardcoded 3-layer system.

## Required Reading (in order)
1. @layers/DYNAMIC-LAYERS-DESIGN.md - Complete design specification and decisions
2. @layers/CLAUDE.md - Current system architecture and context
3. @layers/layers-osc-core.scd - Current implementation to be refactored
4. @setup/vst-management.scd - GUI integration points

## Key Design Principles
- **Name-based OSC paths**: `/group/bass_tuba/note` (stable, efficient)
- **Event-driven updates**: Hook into `~refreshLayerVSTGroups` callback (no polling)
- **O(1) operations**: Add/remove groups without rebuilding all layers
- **Independent navigation**: Each group manages own melody list
- **MIDI modulo cycling**: All groups controllable via 3 rows (index % 3)
- **Generic SynthDef**: Single `\ccEnvelopeGeneric` for all groups

## Implementation Checklist
Refer to "Implementation Checklist" section in DYNAMIC-LAYERS-DESIGN.md

## Critical Implementation Details
1. **Name sanitization**: Remove spaces, special chars for OSC paths
2. **Alphabetical indexing**: Stable ordering for MIDI row assignment
3. **Dictionary-based configs**: `~oscLayers.configs` is Dictionary, not object
4. **7 OSCFuncs per group**: Create/free in pairs with group lifecycle
5. **Preserve backward compat**: Map `layer1/2/3` to first 3 groups alphabetically

## Success Criteria
- [ ] System initializes with N groups (tested with 2, 5, 10)
- [ ] Add group via GUI → layer auto-created
- [ ] Remove group via GUI → layer auto-removed, other layers unaffected
- [ ] OSC paths stable (don't change on add/remove)
- [ ] MIDI rows cycle correctly (group 4 → row 1)
- [ ] Independent melody navigation per group works
- [ ] Chord mode routes across all groups dynamically
- [ ] Backward compatibility: `~layers.configs.layer1` still works

## Common Pitfalls to Avoid
- ❌ Don't use index-based OSC paths (indices shift)
- ❌ Don't recreate all OSCFuncs on group change (only affected groups)
- ❌ Don't use polling Task (use event callbacks)
- ❌ Don't create per-group SynthDefs (use generic parameterized one)
- ❌ Don't forget to update MIDI indices after rebuild

## Testing Approach
1. Start with 0 groups, verify empty system
2. Add 1 group, verify OSC path created
3. Add 2 more groups (3 total), verify MIDI rows 1-3
4. Add 4th group, verify MIDI row cycles to 1
5. Remove group 2, verify others unaffected
6. Test chord mode with 5 groups
7. Test independent melody navigation
8. Test backward compat (`~layers.configs.layer1`)

## Code Style
- Follow existing SuperCollider style (vars at top of blocks)
- Avoid gold plating (minimal, essential code only)
- Use descriptive variable names
- Add concise comments for complex logic
- Test incrementally (don't implement everything at once)

